		<category><![CDATA[reinsurance]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Reinsurance linked investment]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.artemis.bm/?p=151086</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Marsh clients are exploring greater use of third-party capital solutions, including sidecars for liability portfolios, as abundant reinsurance capacity and relatively benign catastrophe losses keep market conditions competitive ahead of the January 1 renewals, according to John Doyle, the firm’s President and Chief Executive Officer. Speaking on Marsh’s Q3 2026 earnings call today, Doyle said [&#8230;]</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/marsh-ceo-flags-client-interest-in-casualty-sidecars-notes-reinsurance-market-softening/">Marsh CEO flags client interest in casualty sidecars, notes reinsurance market softening</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
