					<description><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>At the Convergence 2026 conference in Bermuda this week, CEO&#8217;s of reinsurance companies explained that while property catastrophe rates have declined from recent generational highs they still feel there is adequacy and a runway to make good profits, albeit there are some worrying signs. Ryan Mather, CEO of Ariel Re and Cathal Carr, CEO of [&#8230;]</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/still-runway-to-make-good-cat-profits-but-there-are-some-worrying-signs-convergence-ceo-panel/">Still runway to make good cat profits, but there are some worrying signs: Convergence CEO panel</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
